<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Macquarie enters ASX indices.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Macquarie enters ASX indices.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-10-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Investment bank Macquarie Bank Ltd said on Tuesday it would become part of the Australian Stock Exchange (ASX) All Ordinaries, All Industrials, Banks and Finance, ASX 100 and Trans Tasman indices on October 30.</p>
<p>Macquarie listed its fully paid ordinary shares with the ASX on July 29 after 15 years operation as Hill Samuel Australia Ltd and a further 11 years as the only substantial, Australian-owned investment bank.  </p>
<p>Macquarie said that at current prices, the bank's shares would comprise about 0.32 percent of the All Ordinaries index, 0.45 percent of the All Industrials index and about 1.75 percent of the Banks and Finance index.</p>
<p>Macquarie shares closed one cent firmer at A$7.36.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 373-1800</p>
</text>
